    {
      "id": "fe373ac93a629739dedd59c1e3ef5ac8df0c644a",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1408337055,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Works for me. It scrolls so that the current packet is the last row shown. (Oddly, when I Go To Packet #N, it seems to scroll so that the chosen packet is the next to last packet, but selected.) It might be nicer (but harder to implement, I think) to make it so that the view doesn't really change, or to do something like the intelligent scrollbar/minimap clicking where the current packet is 25% of the way down. But this is certainly good enough and a big improvement.\n\nThere's something similar when changing the layout - for me, that seems to already work with one packet selected, but doesn't work with multiple packets selected (in the latter case, goes back to the first packet.) That is true both with and without this MR.\n\nI think it's correct that we *don't* want to call `scrollViewChanged()`, as in the `goToPacket()` family of functions, because we don't want to change the auto scrolling status in the case of a capture.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-05-28T13:22:13.108Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-06-12T11:16:41.194Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 226640699,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 10822,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1426932188,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think the Go To Packet issue with selecting the next to last packet is because the AccordionFrame is still visible.\n\nI made some changes in !11007 to position the selected packet at center instead of at bottom, which I think is better in most cases.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
