    {
      "id": "52ce6b4191dcffcc6e97953cde84c9a75e4cb2fe",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1408425225,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It looks like the issue with multiple packets selected is related to the changes in b3f240dbf8.\n\nIn `sectionChanged()` we do `cf_unselect_packet()` when selectedRows > 1, and then `rescan_packets()` doesn't have `cf->current_frame` to be able to select it when done.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-05-28T18:24:21.863Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-05-28T18:24:21.863Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 226640699,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 10822,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03b71fecfcd9626dd8079e74f91ee80e655def6c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1415749873,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Clearing `cf->current_frame` when doing a multiselect also has the effect that \"Find Packet\" will start from the first packet in the file, rather than from any of the frames selected. When one packet is selected it starts from that packet.\n\nUser expectation is probably... unclear, but something like either the first packet selected, the last packet select, or the smallest frame number among all the packets selected. (Or, much more annoying to do, \"Is it possible if multiple packets are selected to do Find Packet searching only through those packets, not the whole file?\")\n\nIn `sectionChanged()`, after the `cf_unselect_packet()`, maybe there should be a `cf->current_frame = packet_list_model_->getRowFdata(row)` for some row - not sure which one, maybe the minimum row in the `QList<int> rows`? Is there anything that actually has a problem if `cf->current_frame` is set but there's no active tree? In some brief testing, I haven't found an issue.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-06-02T02:21:03.878Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-06-02T02:21:03.878Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 226640699,
